DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The hhoossttaappdd__ccllii utility is a text-based frontend program for interacting
     with hostapd(8).  It is used to query the current status.

     The hhoossttaappdd__ccllii utility can show the current authentication status, dot11
     and dot1x MIBs, etc.

     The hhoossttaappdd__ccllii utility supports two modes: interactive and command line.
     Both modes share the same command set.

     Interactive mode is started when hhoossttaappdd__ccllii is executed without any pa‐
     rameters on the command line.  Commands are then entered from the con‐
     trolling terminal in response to the hhoossttaappdd__ccllii prompt.  In command line
     mode, the same commands are entered as command line arguments.

CCOOMMMMAANNDDSS
     The following commands may be supplied on the command line or at a prompt
     when operating interactively.

     mmiibb     Report MIB variables (dot1x, dot11) for the current interface.

     ssttaa _a_d_d_r
             Report the MIB variables for the associated station with MAC ad‐
             dress _a_d_d_r.

     aallll__ssttaa
             Report the MIB variables for all associated stations.

     hheellpp    Show usage help.

     iinntteerrffaaccee [_i_f_n_a_m_e]
             Show available interfaces and/or set the current interface when
             multiple are available.

     lleevveell _d_e_b_u_g___l_e_v_e_l
             Change the debugging level in hostapd(8).  Larger numbers gener‐
             ate more messages.

     lliicceennssee
             Display the full license for hhoossttaappdd__ccllii.

     qquuiitt    Exit hhoossttaappdd__ccllii.

